Vendored graph-runtime-wasm patch
=================================

Upstream: https://github.com/graphprotocol/graph-node
Revision: 77823b5a7adc4eac4abf03202c8dd7cb00dea31d (tag v0.44.0)
Path:     runtime/wasm
Licence:  MIT OR Apache-2.0 (LICENSE-MIT and LICENSE-APACHE copied verbatim)

Why this exists
---------------

The order in which a mapping called `store.set` is not observable through
graph-node's public API: `EntityCache` collapses writes into a `HashMap` and
`as_modifications` iterates it arbitrarily. It *is* observable beside the
proof-of-indexing writes in `HostExports`, which already emit one event per
store call, in call order, and which the PoI itself hashes. This patch adds an
optional recorder there and nothing else.

The default is `None`, so an unconfigured runtime behaves exactly as upstream
does. The patch is additive and intended to be upstreamable.

What changed
------------

  src/op_recorder.rs   new file: the `EntityOpRecorder` trait
  src/lib.rs           export the module and the two public names
  src/host_exports.rs  one optional field, one setter, three call sites
  src/host.rs          carry the recorder from the builder into `HostExports`

Everything else under src/ is byte-identical to upstream. Cargo.toml differs
structurally because upstream inherits version, edition, several dependency
versions and its lint table from the graph-node workspace, which does not exist
here; upstream's manifest is kept beside it as Cargo.toml.upstream.

Regenerate with:

  diff -ruN <graph-node-checkout>/runtime/wasm/src \
            mapping-host/vendor/graph-runtime-wasm/src

